---
/*
 * The immutable copy of the OpenE2EE Relay Beta Service Limits, version
 * 2026-08-26. The Relay Service Terms incorporate this document, so a
 * customer who filed the terms must be able to file the version of this
 * document they pointed at. This page is a literal snapshot: the document
 * text is inlined here, and the page must never import the live version
 * constants or the live page, or an edit to /legal/relay-beta-limits would
 * reach the archive that exists to escape it. This copy is the text
 * /legal/relay-beta-limits rendered on 2026-09-10, immediately before the
 * upload-authorization window was restated as a ceiling in version
 * 2026-09-10; the 2026-08-30 environment rename and the 2026-09-07 pricing-
 * link change are included, since no customer filed the text between. A new
 * version means a new dated page beside this one, never an edit.
 * tests/legal-pages.test.mjs enforces that this source stays decoupled from
 * the live page and the live version constants.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import {
  ARTICLE_COLUMN,
  ARTICLE_HEADER,
  ARTICLE_META,
  BACK_LINK,
  CONTAINER,
  LEAD,
  LEGAL_PIN,
} from '../../../lib/recipes';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Beta limits 2026-08-26"
  description="Frozen copy of the OpenE2EE Relay Beta Service Limits, version 2026-08-26."
  canonical="/legal/relay-beta-limits/2026-08-26"
>
  <article>
    <header class={ARTICLE_HEADER}>
      <div class:list={[CONTAINER, ARTICLE_COLUMN]}>
        <a class={BACK_LINK} href="/legal">Legal</a>
        <h1>OpenE2EE Relay Beta Service Limits</h1>
        <p class={LEAD}>The launch boundary for capacity, support, and service commitments.</p>
        <p class={ARTICLE_META}>
          <span>Effective August 26, 2026</span>
          <span>Version 2026-08-26</span>
        </p>
        <p class={LEGAL_PIN}>
          The Relay terms incorporate this document. The permanent copy of this version is at{' '}
          <a href="/legal/relay-beta-limits/2026-08-26"><code>/legal/relay-beta-limits/2026-08-26</code></a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class:list={[CONTAINER, ARTICLE_COLUMN]}>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Service status</h2>
        <p>
          Relay remains a beta until OpenE2EE announces general availability. The Development
          environment and Free production plan have no service-level agreement. Paid beta support and operational
          controls are those shown in the order. No uptime credit, response-time commitment, data
          residency promise, BAA, or production recovery objective applies unless a signed order
          form states it.
        </p>

        <h2>Plan and protocol limits</h2>
        <p>
          The current plan capacities and exact meter definitions are at{' '}
          <a href="/pricing#relay-plans">Relay pricing</a>. All plans support the same Relay protocol
          capabilities. A plan does not unlock or remove groups, attachments, sealed sender,
          multi-device delivery, or push wakes.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Direct encrypted envelope: 256 KiB maximum.</li>
          <li>Mailbox: 3,000 accepted messages maximum.</li>
          <li>Group encrypted body: 96 KiB plus a 512-byte prefix.</li>
          <li>Group delivery: up to 5,000 destination devices in 100-destination fan-out pages.</li>
          <li>Attachment upload URL: 15 minutes maximum.</li>
          <li>Completed attachment retention: 30 days maximum.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Capacity and change control</h2>
        <p>
          A hard cap rejects new work without changing already accepted encrypted content. OpenE2EE
          can reduce abusive or unsafe traffic, repair a service incident, or change pre-release
          limits with reasonable notice when practicable. A material paid-plan change applies under
          the accepted service terms and recorded order.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
